usb_anchor_urb(urb, &parent->rx_submitted);
rc = usb_submit_urb(urb, GFP_ATOMIC);
/* No unanchor on submission failure */
Reason:
After re-anchoring the URB, if `usb_submit_urb()` fails, the URB remains anchored in `parent->rx_submitted`. This prevents `usb_kill_anchored_urbs()` in `gs_can_close()` from ever completing, causing an infinite loop.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
rc = usb_submit_urb(urb, GFP_ATOMIC);
+if (!rc)
+    return;
+usb_unanchor_urb(urb);
/* Additional error handling remains */
Reason:
The added `if (!rc) return;` ensures that on successful submission, execution returns immediately without falling into the error path. The subsequent `usb_unanchor_urb(urb)` unanchors the URB on submission failure, preventing the infinite loop in `gs_can_close()`. The info message added in the error path aids debugging.

